  "notes": "All 104 matches and all 48 teams present and validated (round-robin completeness, match numbers 1-104 contiguous, W-links reference earlier matches). kickoff_local is the venue-LOCAL time from Wikipedia per-group pages, each of which carried its UTC offset (fixing the IANA tz). Mexico abolished DST in 2022, so Mexico City and Guadalajara (Estadio Akron, Zapopan) are America/Mexico_City = UTC-6 in summer; Monterrey (Estadio BBVA, Guadalupe) is America/Monterrey = UTC-6. US/Canada venues are on DST (EDT/CDT/PDT). Official FIFA match numbering is CHRONOLOGICAL by kickoff (per ESPN), NOT grouped by group letter (Sky Sports' per-group numbering differs and was not used for the 'num' field). Knockout team slots are placeholders: '1A'/'2B'=group winner/runner-up, '3rd A/B/C/D/F'=a best-third-placed team from one of those groups (FIFA Annex C, 495 combos), 'W##'/'L##'=winner/loser of that match number. Group-stage home/away designations are nominal (no home advantage implied beyond hosts). NOTE: ESPN listed match 16 (Iran v New Zealand) as the day's late game; Wikipedia gives its local kickoff as 18:00 PDT (=21:00 ET), which is used here as it is internally consistent with the page's stated UTC-7 offset."
